{"kind":"assert","text":"C2 carry, on ruling b1b1d492. The checker's review b45bb16a found that\na throw of `Unheld` does not reach the client. Three places in\n`packages/derive/src` catch it first: `run` and `unjudged` in\n`marks.ts`, and `readRetainedUses` in `retained-use.ts`.\n\nThe ruling for C2 changes in one place. The replica's `Own` throws\n`Unheld` and also records each throw. After each call of a judge or of\nthe fold, the client reads the record and then clears it. A record\nthat is not empty makes the prediction `not-judged` or stops the\nreplica, whatever the call returned. No catch site of\n`packages/derive` changes.\n\nThe list that you owe before C2 code gains two parts: the ports of\n`RetainedOwn` (`retainedRow`, `retainedBirth`), and each catch site\nthat can wrap a read of `Own`. C2 adds one test for each catch site: a\nreplica that lacks a held entry or copy reads `not-judged` there.\n\nThe state seed note states the rule in section 3 and section 9, at\nhead 485f867e. It is in review (9e219191).","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}